1|0@darksouls3^1440834875#cujk1hr:Ateaga$:Lucky you for trying it out so many times! I had to come back 3 times before they finally let me in the line. After waiting an hour and half to play, I was not dissapointed in my time. The combat is a step below the speed of Bloodborne but faster than the others. All the animations felt extremely responsive and well executed so it was easy to dodge a lot of incoming blows. I was able to make it to the boss fight fairly easy in the 10 minutes they gave me, and when it ran out, they let me continue beating it. Got it down to 3/4 health before it took out its other sword and I mistimed its combo and died. I didn't explore much as I was sick of seeing everyone die so early to stupid things and wanted to see where the boss was. I really enjoyed the enemy variety as well. There was a good mix of single harder enemies, or lots of easy undead to take down. I liked it better than 2 which I felt like most enemy placement wasn't coherent in some places. Did you get the key above near the dragon?
